{
 "cases": [
  {
   "i": 15990,
   "title": "Staging Payment Gateway: HTTP 429 and empty responses causing webhook failure",
   "description": "We are seeing issues with the Payment Gateway v2 in our EU-West staging environment. When making API calls, we occasionally receive an empty response body, and frequently hit HTTP 429 errors. This seems to be causing our webhook delivery system to exhaust its retries because the initial calls fail or return nothing useful. We have approximately 47 test users impacted by this flow. Can you check if there are rate limit changes or backend issues on the staging cluster?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15991,
   "title": "Production APAC: Users being charged twice for single transactions",
   "description": "We are experiencing a high-impact issue in the production APAC region where customers are reporting duplicate charges on their statements. About 305 users have reported this so far. We've looked into it and we think this is definitely a resource exhaustion problem on your end—likely the database or compute instances are running out of capacity, causing the transaction handler to retry the payment capture without checking if the first one succeeded. Please confirm if your cluster is under-resourced and scale it up immediately."
  },
  {
   "i": 15992,
   "title": "SSO Module: Provisioning hangs and creates duplicate accounts",
   "description": "In our production ME environment, the SSO Integration Module is behaving inconsistently. We have a few cases where user provisioning gets stuck in a 'pending' state and never completes. Worse, when an admin attempts to force-create or manually intervene, it results in duplicate account entries being created for the same email address. This affects about 19 internal users currently. We need to know why the provisioning queue is stalling and why the uniqueness constraint isn't catching the duplicate creation attempts."
  },
  {
   "i": 15993,
   "title": "Staging ANZ: Cohort Builder export issues - duplicates and truncation",
   "description": "We are running exports in the Cohort Builder on our ANZ staging setup. The resulting files seem corrupted in two ways: first, we are seeing duplicate records appearing multiple times in the output CSV. Second, the file appears to be truncated, stopping abruptly before all expected data is written. It's unclear if the logic for de-duplication is failing or if the file writing process itself is being interrupted. Only 2 users are affected so far (low impact), but the data quality is unusable. Can you check if there's an issue with the export worker or the underlying storage connection?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15994,
   "title": "CRITICAL: EU-Central SSO error page and expired password reset links",
   "description": "This is a critical issue affecting our production EU-Central environment. Users attempting to log in via SSO are being presented with a generic error page instead of being redirected. Additionally, any password reset links sent out are showing as 'expired' immediately upon clicking, even for new emails. This is blocking access for over 12,000 users. We suspect a configuration mismatch or an invalidation of tokens/links on the SSO side. Please investigate urgently."
  },
  {
   "i": 15995,
   "title": "MFA not showing up",
   "description": "Hey, is anyone else seeing that the MFA prompt isn't appearing in the sandbox? We tried logging in a few times in EU-West but it just skipped it or something. Not a big deal yet but it's weird. Let me know if you know why."
  },
  {
   "i": 15996,
   "title": "Staging EU-West: Bulk import completely failed",
   "description": "We attempted a bulk import of users into the staging environment, but it failed entirely with no partial successes. We aren't sure if the issue is with the core SSO module processing the data or if it's related to the Social Login Connector integration since those accounts also have linked social IDs. The import logs just say 'failed' without specifying which part of the pipeline broke. 48 users were supposed to be imported. Can you help us determine if this is an SSO configuration issue or a connector handshake problem?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15997,
   "title": "Queue Manager slow",
   "description": "The Queue Manager in EU-Central production is being really slow lately. It's taking forever for things to process. We have about 250 people complaining that their actions aren't reflecting. Is there a backlog or something? Need this looked at as it's causing big delays."
  },
  {
   "i": 15998,
   "title": "Analytics config not working",
   "description": "Tried changing some settings on the Analytics Dashboard in APAC prod but it doesn't seem to be taking effect. Also getting some warning about config drift? Only one of us is trying to use this specific view right now so low impact, but it's annoying. Can you check?"
  },
  {
   "i": 15999,
   "title": "Webhooks failing in staging",
   "description": "In LATAM staging, our webhooks from the SSO module are retrying and then just giving up. We're seeing 'retries exhausted' errors. About 32 users are affected but we haven't dug into the exact error codes or timestamps yet because it's intermittent. Just want to flag that the event delivery isn't working reliably."
  },
  {
   "i": 16000,
   "title": "Access denied errors in ME staging",
   "description": "We are getting 'Access Denied' errors when trying to access certain resources in the SSO Integration Module (ME staging). This is happening for about 46 users. We honestly have no idea why this is happening. We think it might just be insufficient information on our end or maybe a permission misconfiguration, but we can't tell what the actual root cause is. It's definitely an issue with the access control layer but we can't pinpoint if it's the user, the role, or the resource. Please investigate."
  },
  {
   "i": 16001,
   "title": "US-West Production: Audit logs missing entries",
   "description": "We have noticed that the audit log in our Analytics Dashboard (US-West production) is incomplete. Specific user actions that we know occurred are missing from the log stream. We have about 59 users whose activity should be recorded but isn't appearing. This is a moderate impact as it affects our compliance reporting. Can you check if there is a delay in the ingestion pipeline or if events are being dropped for specific user segments?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16002,
   "title": "APAC Analytics Dashboard: Partial outage and pod restarts",
   "description": "Our Analytics Dashboard in the APAC production region is experiencing a partial outage. Users report that some widgets load and others time out. We suspect the backend is unstable because we are observing repeated pod restarts on our monitoring tools. This affects approximately 53 users. We need to know if the repeated restarts are due to a memory issue or a dependency failure within the dashboard service."
  },
  {
   "i": 16003,
   "title": "Fee Analyzer issues: Overcharges and declined payments",
   "description": "We are seeing strange behavior with the Fee Analyzer in the US-East sandbox. Some transactions are being flagged with incorrect fees (overcharge) and subsequently, the payment processing is declining the transaction. About 18 test cases are affected. It looks like the fee calculation logic is producing invalid amounts that exceed the transaction limit or trigger fraud rules, causing the decline. Can you look into the fee calculation engine?"
  },
  {
   "i": 16004,
   "title": "EU-Central Production: Onboarding Wizard stuck and creating duplicates",
   "description": "The Onboarding Wizard in our EU-Central production environment has issues with user provisioning. We see cases where the provisioning step gets stuck and never finishes. In other instances, it creates duplicate account records for the same user during the onboarding flow. This impacts about 25 users currently. We need to understand why the wizard state is persisting in 'stuck' mode and why the duplicate check is failing during the account creation step."
  }
 ]
